Yeah, `SetVolumeOwnership()` is a little coarse for what we would want.  My fear is that we do something "manual" here and miss something or maybe later something changes there and it works everywhere EXCEPT here.  Doubly so because this same problem exists in projected, secret, configmap, and downwardapi volumes.  You can't just fix it in one place.

What if we changed `SetVolumeOwnership` to take an optional "subpath" argument and then changed `AtomicWriter.Write()` to take a "set permissions" function.  Something like:

